# Scan notes & known doc drift

Observations from reading the code directly, beyond what `CLAUDE.md` states.
Trust the **code** over any prose when they disagree.

## Known drift

- **`_GNORM` comment is stale.** `engine.py` still says "field std ~0.27, clips
  ~3.6%". `CLAUDE.md` records this was re-measured to **std ~0.45, clips ~18%**
  and the old note was simply wrong. The constant (0.55) is correct; only the
  inline justification is outdated.
- **"79 checks" is a runtime count.** `verify.py` has ~67 static `check()` call
  sites; the higher figure counts checks inside loops.
- **`edge_jitter` default drift.** `params.py` help says default 0.3 wanders
  "±0.4px" while some prose says "±0.227px typical" — the 0.227 figure referred
  to the *old* 0.6px cap; current `_JITTER_MAX=3.0`, so the code/help is right.

## Confirmed architecture facts (useful shortcuts)

- Renders are **serialised** behind `_RENDER_LOCK` in `main.py` — one GPU, and
  the UI only needs the newest preview.
- Endpoints doing tensor work are sync `def` (not `async`) on purpose, so
  Starlette runs them in a threadpool and one slow render can't block the loop.
- Uploads/jobs live **in process memory** (12-upload LRU, `_reap()`); `/api/source`
  PNG is encoded once per upload and cached.
- Preview tile size is **1536** (amortises fixed overlap); export uses **1024**.
- Input: **JPEG/PNG only, 30MB max**; MPO (multi-frame JPEG) accepted, frame 0
  read. TIFF dropped, RAW not implemented (needs rawpy/LibRaw).

## Not converted from Claude config

- `.claude/settings.local.json` is a **permission allowlist** (bash/read globs).
  It has no direct Cursor project equivalent here; Cursor CLI permissions live
  in `~/.cursor/cli-config.json` (global). Left as-is — ask before migrating.
- `CLAUDE.md` / `TOPIC.md` / `README.md` are kept as the **deep reference**;
  these `.mdc` rules are the fast-catchup layer distilled from them.
